1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:07,200
Error handling in doeff. A failure is handled like everything else: with an effect and a handler.

2
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:16,300
First, run itself. It gives back what the program returns, as it is: here, the string DOEFF.

3
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:22,400
When the program raises, run raises the same exception. There is no wrapper around either.

4
00:00:24,350 --> 00:00:31,550
To keep a failure as a value, doeff has two kinds of result. Ok holds a value. Err holds an exception.

5
00:00:32,850 --> 00:00:37,200
Ok is true and Err is false, and both match by pattern.

6
00:00:39,350 --> 00:00:43,400
This is app. It turns the text raw into a count.

7
00:00:43,950 --> 00:00:48,750
First it tries parse count on raw. The result is parsed.

8
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,650
If parsed is Ok, it logs the count and returns it.

9
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:58,300
If parsed is Err, it logs the failure and returns zero.

10
00:00:58,850 --> 00:01:03,950
Try is an effect. At the yield, app pauses and hands Try to a handler.

11
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:09,450
The try handler runs parse count inside itself.

12
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:16,900
int raises on the text "not a number". The handler catches the exception and wraps it in Err.

13
00:01:17,450 --> 00:01:24,700
Then it resumes k with that Err. app takes the Err case, logs the failure, and returns zero.

14
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:31,400
Without the try handler in the stack, Try is unhandled. It is a handler like any other.

15
00:01:32,250 --> 00:01:35,700
Try keeps three promises when it meets other effects.

16
00:01:36,450 --> 00:01:41,900
One: no rollback. The Put before the failure stays, so counter is one.

17
00:01:42,450 --> 00:01:49,550
Two: when the failure passes through Local, Local still restores the environment. key is outer again.

18
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:56,650
Three: Try inside Try keeps both layers. You get Ok of Ok, or Ok of Err.

19
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:02,900
load raises FileNotFoundError for the path it is given.

20
00:02:03,450 --> 00:02:09,800
boom yields load of config.toml, and returns what it gives.

21
00:02:10,350 --> 00:02:15,350
app yields Try of boom, to keep a failure as a value.

22
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:20,350
run runs app under the try handler, and returns the result.

23
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:25,000
The result is an Err. Its exception still has its traceback.

24
00:02:25,550 --> 00:02:30,200
Read its frames from the top. The first is attempt, inside the try handler.

25
00:02:30,750 --> 00:02:34,250
Next is boom, at its yield of load.

26
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:38,100
Last is load, where the error was raised.

27
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:48,150
Failures in doeff: Try asks, a handler answers with Ok or Err, and your code decides what comes next.
